{
 "format": 1,
 "label": "Multi-shot film: one look in every shot (FLUX.3 + Qwen board + LTX canny)",
 "description": "A film of several shots with one look. Each shot is a timeline marker bound to a camera (Shot 1, 2, 3). Shot 1's first frame becomes the hero keyframe (FLUX.3 Klein); a Material Board cut from it (swatches, no layout) gives shots 2 and 3 the same materials through Qwen 2.1 edit, while each keeps its own composition. LTX 2.5 canny films every shot's clay animation from its keyframe (seed 7), and the Film node puts the clips end to end in the ComfyQ Film scene (Render Film writes the MP4). One Look prompt is shared by every shot. Tested on the cliff house (2026-10-22, docs/multi-shot.md).",
 "made": "2026-10-22 01:46",
